# Ceph Single‑Page Ops Cheat Sheet

> Copy–paste friendly. Each command includes **why it exists**.

---

## 1️⃣ Safe Removal of a Node (example: node1)

### Check cluster health (must NOT be HEALTH_ERR)

```bash
ceph -s                      # Overall cluster status
ceph health detail           # Detailed health issues
```

### Identify OSDs on node1

```bash
ceph osd tree                # Shows OSD → host mapping
```

### Mark OSDs OUT (triggers data rebalance)

```bash
ceph osd out osd.0           # Stop placing new data on osd.0
ceph osd out osd.1           # Data is replicated elsewhere
```

### Monitor rebalance and PG state

```bash
ceph -s                      # Watch recovery/backfill
ceph pg stat                 # PG states (wait for active+clean)
```

### Remove OSD daemons (after PGs are clean)

```bash
ceph orch daemon rm osd.0    # Remove OSD container & config
ceph orch daemon rm osd.1
```

### Remove MON (ensure quorum remains ≥ 3)

```bash
ceph quorum_status           # Check MON quorum
ceph orch daemon rm mon.node1
```

### Remove MGR

```bash
ceph orch daemon rm mgr.node1
```

### Remove host from cluster

```bash
ceph orch host rm node1      # Final cleanup
```

