1️⃣ MON (Monitor)
What MON does

👉 Maintains cluster state & consensus

MON stores:

Cluster map

OSD map

MON map

CRUSH map

Authentication info (cephx)

Key properties

Uses Paxos (consensus algorithm)

Needs quorum (odd number)

Why MON is critical

Without MON quorum → cluster freezes

No IO decisions can be made

Commands related to MON
ceph quorum_status        # Who is in quorum
ceph mon dump             # Monitor map

Failure scenario

Lose 1 MON out of 5 → OK

Lose quorum → ❌ cluster stuck

2️⃣ MGR (Manager)
What MGR does

👉 Real-time monitoring, metrics, and control logic

MGR handles:

Dashboard

Prometheus exporter

Orchestration (cephadm)

Balancer

Telemetry

PG autoscaler

Key properties

Active + Standby

Stateless (can fail safely)

Why MGR exists

Before MGR:

MONs were overloaded
Now:

MON = critical state

MGR = operational intelligence

Commands related to MGR
ceph mgr services        # Dashboard, prometheus URLs
ceph mgr dump            # Active/standby mgr

Failure scenario

Active MGR dies → standby takes over

Cluster IO continues normally

3️⃣ OSD (Object Storage Daemon)
What OSD does

👉 Stores actual data + handles replication

OSD responsibilities:

Store objects on disk (NVMe/HDD)

Replication

Recovery

Backfill

Scrubbing

Heartbeats

Key properties

One OSD ≈ one disk

Uses BlueStore backend

Talks directly to other OSDs

Why OSD is performance-critical

Latency

Throughput

Data durability

Commands related to OSD
ceph osd tree            # OSD layout
ceph osd df              # Disk usage

Failure scenario

One OSD dies → data re-replicated

Too many OSDs down → data unavailable

One Table That Locks It In Your Brain
Component	Purpose	Stores Data?	HA Model	If it fails
MON	Cluster truth	❌	Quorum	Cluster stuck
MGR	Metrics & control	❌	Active/Standby	Transparent
OSD	Data storage	✅	Replication	Rebuild
One-Line Memory Trick (Interview Gold)

MON decides what the cluster looks like
MGR decides how the cluster behaves
OSD does the actual work

Bonus: Who talks to whom?
Client → MON (map)
Client → OSD (IO)
MGR ← OSDs (metrics)
MON ↔ MON (quorum)
OSD ↔ OSD (replication)

